      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e GoogleTest does not run tests in parallel and you have SetUp() and TearDown() starting/stopping the kumquat instance so there should only ever be a single instance. \n\nNuked `eglInitializeKumquat` + `vkInitializeKumquat` in the latest patch, since it was based on the assumption GoogleTest was multi-threaded, which isn\u0027t correct.\n\n\u003e Then have VirtGpuKumquatDevice keep the `std::shared_ptr\u003cKumaquatServer\u003e` as a member. \n\nI added a `KumquatInstance` wrapper in `common/end2end`.  `VirtGpuKumquatDevice` is envisioned as a gfxstream guest internal, and should be only connecting and sending requiests to Kumquat, not managing it.  \n\nI do agree that launching a `KumquatInstance` for every test is unnecessary.  We probably only need a `KumquatInstance` for every test suite (since a test-suite can change the arguments to gfxstream, and hence test behavior).  That is left for a future refactor, since the prior behavior was to call `rutabaga_init` for every test, which is also unnecessary.",
      "parentUuid": "593b6af5_35e82067",
