      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I do agree that launching a KumquatInstance for every test is unnecessary\n\nErr, I think launching a `KumquatInstance` is the correct way to go so that each test gets a clean state and previous tests can not affect the current test.\n\nThis was just about potentially not having to manually do the `mKumquatInstance.reset();` inside of `TearDown()` because it would happen naturally as a part each `VirtGpuKumquatDevice` being destructed.\n\nI think what this change has now is a good middle ground considering you want `VirtGpuKumquatDevice`/\"the guest\" to not manage the kumaquat server which seems reasonable.",
