      "writtenOn": "2024-08-09T17:44:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I still left the comment about `SetUpTestSuite` + `TearDownTestSuite`, since *in theory* each test in suite should create/teardown a new virtio-gpu context and associated resources.  If a prior run leaves state, that\u0027s probably a bug in gfxstream.  \n\nI  think the main benefit of `SetUpTestSuite` + `TearDownTestSuite`.  Right now, the tests take ~7 minutes.  It could be faster if expensive calls (`stream_renderer_init` + `stream_renderer_teardown`) aren\u0027t always made.  But that said, I have no intention of personally doing that optimization.",
